        "David Huang",
        "Eric A. Swanson",
        "James G. Fujimoto"
      ],
      "assessment": {
        "nobel_worthiness": "Optical coherence tomography opened a non-invasive high-resolution imaging modality with extraordinary practical and scientific reach.",
        "attribution": "Huang, Swanson and Fujimoto form a coherent, limited group associated with the original invention and demonstration.",
        "maturity": "OCT is independently established worldwide, especially in ophthalmology, and its impact is unambiguous.",
        "uncertainties": [
          "The committee would need to weigh a strongly biomedical application against other physics advances."
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "rank": 6,
